<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stjepan Vukčić Kosača</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1404">1404</a>–<a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stjepan Vukčić Kosača was the most powerful noble of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> in the mid-15th century, inheriting Hum and the coast from his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandalj-hranic-kosaca">Sandalj Hranić</a> in 1435. Often at odds with the Bosnian kings and Ragusa, in 1448 he took the title Herceg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-sava">Saint Sava</a>, from which his lands took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> conquered most of his territory before his death in 1466.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stjepan-vukcic-kosaca.jpg" alt="Stjepan Vukčić Kosača" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matěj Baťha · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Blagaj_fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
